    "done_when": "With the plan subsection with id definitions-2026-09-29 governs wherever the section text leaves room: a new module imas_ambix/agent/cache_estimate.py exposes a function over request receipts that counts a request as a hit when the same caller's previous request to the same model arrived strictly within the cache lifetime, the caller being run_id when a non-empty string, else coordinator_session when a non-empty string, else none (never a hit), and returns h as hit prompt tokens over all prompt tokens, timing each request's arrival as its timestamp minus its duration; tests in tests/test_cache_estimate.py pin h on a fixture, including a gap exactly equal to the lifetime counting as a miss, a caller-less request counting as a miss and two models not chaining; a report at the write path states h over the most recent 7 days of ~/public/imas-ambix/requests.jsonl at the lifetime of the provider serving most of the first measurement's responses (Novita, per /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/0c4316b2-553f-4a0a-ae02-c42d88de747c/third-party-hit-rate/third-party-hit-rate.json) with that provider's page and access date, plus sensitivity rows at 300 s and 3600 s, the caller share and the row count; gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_cache_estimate.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0",
